 HISTORY                                                          8105 1451
 -------                                                          8105 1451
    This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction       8105 1451
    Physics (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. 8105 1451
    The thermal scattering law data for Uranium in Uranium        8105 1451
    Carbide was developed using ab initio lattice dynamics        8105 1451
    (AILD)[1,2]. Ten temperatures are available in this library.  8105 1451
    The Full Law Analysis Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) system   8105 1451
    was used to produce File 7 MT = 2, 4 data for Uranium in UC   8105 1451
    [3]. MAT=8105 and ZA=8205 are used for U in UC (5% enriched). 8105 1451
    Elemental AWR and cross sections were computed from           8105 1451
    ENDF/B-VIII.0 MF=3 MT=2 nuclide evaluations [4] at 1e-5eV     8105 1451
     with C-12 updated to reflect a mass of exactly 12 amu.       8105 1451
